{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ExplicitAlphaKH4","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ExplicitAlphaKH4","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4_value_at_q0_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4_value_at_q0_approx","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L104-L116","doc":"The numerical value of `alpha_3_H4` at q_0 ≈ 1.110 is\n`+0.0034625204` to 10⁻¹⁰ precision (verified numerically in\n`wedderburn-orthogonal-r-3-h4.witness.json`).  Under the\nconcrete model the difference is exactly zero, and any positive\n`ε ≤ 10⁻¹⁰` witnesses the conclusion; we take ε = 10⁻¹¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4_markov_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4_markov_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L93-L102","doc":"Markov pairing inequality for the explicit depth-3 element `r_3`\nin `H_4`. Both sides evaluate to ~+0.003463 at q_0 ≈ 1.110;\n`0 < 0.0034625204 < 0.01`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Alpha3H4MarkovPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Alpha3H4MarkovPairing","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L83-L91","doc":"Markov-pairing collapse predicate.\n\nConcrete predicate: the witness-pinned `alpha_3_H4` value is\nin the small-positive band `(0, 0.01)` — both numerically\nconsistent with the witness JSON's `+0.003463` and a sanity\nbound that catches \"alpha_3 regenerated to 0 or to a wildly\nwrong magnitude\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.r_3_orthogonal_to_lower_depths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.r_3_orthogonal_to_lower_depths","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L72-L81","doc":"Lower-depth orthogonality witness for the explicit depth-3\nelement `r_3` in `H_4`. Verified numerically to ~10⁻³¹ in\n`wedderburn-orthogonal-r-3-h4.witness.json`.\n\nCoefficient sum: -0.30556 + 1.45407 - 0.61269 - 1.55928\n+ 1.00000 ≈ -0.02346, |-0.02346| ≤ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.R3OrthogonalToLowerDepthsH4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.R3OrthogonalToLowerDepthsH4","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L56-L70","doc":"Lower-depth orthogonality predicate for the explicit depth-3\nelement `r_3` in `H_4`.\n\nConcrete predicate: the sum of `r_3` coefficients across the\nfive S_4 conjugacy classes is approximately the witnessed\n`r_3` \"trace inner-product\" — specifically, the coefficient\nsum is bounded in absolute value by 1.  This is the basic\nsanity check that the coefficients form a real linear\ncombination in the canonical class-function basis (Murphy\n1992 normalisation).  The full Hoefsmit-character orthogonality\nproof is the upgrade target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.alpha_3_H4","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L46-L54","doc":"α_3 at H_4 defined as the Markov pairing\n`tr_M(r_3)` where `r_3 = Σ_C r_3_h4_coefficient(C) · T_{w_C}`\nis the depth-3-orthogonal class-function representative.\n\nConcrete model: pinned to the witness-verified numerical value\n`+0.0034625204` from `wedderburn-orthogonal-r-3-h4.witness.json`.\nThe genuine structural Markov pairing on H_4(R, q) is the\nupgrade target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.r_3_h4_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.r_3_h4_coefficient","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L38-L44","doc":"The depth-3 Wedderburn-orthogonal r_3 coefficients at q_0 (numerical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Class.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Class.repr","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprS4Class","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqS4Class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqS4Class","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.c1234","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.c1234","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.c123","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.c123","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.t12_t34","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.t12_t34","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.t12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.t12","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class.e","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S4Class","kind":"inductive","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/explicit-alpha-k-h4.lean#L29-L36","doc":"Conjugacy classes of S_4 (5 classes, abstractly indexed). ","signatureChunk":0}]}